usqr-s: x * x, for x from 0 to 31.
Cells 82-98. To call it, load x into the accumulator and JMP 82.
It returns x * x in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99.
Size 17 cells. It runs at most 289 instructions, 149.5 on average, counted from cell 82 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 82     696      STO 96   cells 82-84: the call: store x, and copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98
 83     199      CLA 99
 84     698      STO 98
 85     404      SFT 04   cells 85-94: s = 0 by SFT 04; then for c = x down to 1, s = s + 2c - 1
 86     695      STO 95
 87     196      CLA 96
 88     700      SUB 00
 89     397      TAC 97
 90     696      STO 96
 91     296      ADD 96
 92     200      ADD 00
 93     295      ADD 95
 94     886      JMP 86
 95     000      data: the sum s
 96     000      data: x, counted down to 0
 97     195      CLA 95   cell 97: the sum into the accumulator
 98     000               set on every call: the jump back to the caller
